The 1911–12 Scottish football season was [[Celtic F.C.|Celtic]]'s 24th season of competitive football, in which they competed in the [[Scottish First Division]].<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.londonhearts.com/scores/a1910/celtic1912.htm|title=Results for Celtic for 1911-12|website=www.londonhearts.com}}</ref> They finished the league campaign runners-up to [[Rangers F.C.|Rangers]]. Celtic successfully defended their [[Scottish Cup]] trophy as they beat Clyde FC in the final, 2-0. It was Celtic's 18th major domestic honour.

This was the first season as captain for right half [[James Young (footballer, born 1882)|Jim Young]], as half back [[Jimmy Hay]] left the club to play for [[Newcastle United F.C.|Newcastle United]]. Young had been with Celtic since 1903 and was the sixth player to captain the club.

Celtic also won the [[Glasgow Charity Cup|Glasgow Merchants' Charity Cup]] this season.

